  "uprn": "200003972579",
  "decision_date": "28/03/2002",
  "description": "Demolition of existing building and construction of 43 self contained flats on five floors, with ground floor B1 and/or  A2 uses  and showroom,  with 30 car parking spaces.",
  "site_name": "Chiswick Apartments, 548-550",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "02/03/2001",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "W4 5RG",
  "street_name": "Chiswick High Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "27/03/2005",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - No fans, louvres, ducts or other external plant shall be installed without the prior approval of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of             to 8am to 6pm on Mondays to Friday and 8am to 1pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - No development shall take place until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority a plan indicating the positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected.  The boundary treatment shall be completed before  the building  is or in accordance with a timetable agreed in writing with the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 8 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of refuse or waste have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing of refuse or waste shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 9 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for protecting the proposed residential accommodation from excessive external noise shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and any works which form part of such a scheme shall be completed before any part of the development is first occupied or used.",
    "Condition : 10 - Before the development commences details of parking (including spaces for people with disabilities) shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the spaces shown on the approved drawing shall be available for use before first occupation of any part of the development.",
    "Condition : 11 - All parking spaces provided in accordance with approved plans shall be permanently available only for residents of the flats and not be used for any other purposes.\r\n(Reason: To ensure that the parking spaces are only available for use of residentswithin the development).",
    "Condition : 12 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoling or re-enacting that order) no telecommunication equipment shall be installed on the exterior of the building without the prior writtin approval of the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
